From 5aac2f7fca91eeb64acf72ef2efa416669d24acc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 14:45:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] .13 Signal Decision Engine: recognize mirrored short
 candidate, support full coin universe

Recognizes both FROZEN_CANDIDATE (BEAR x LOW ATR x POSITIVE bar-2) and the
newly-defined MIRROR_CANDIDATE (BULL_OR_NEUTRAL x LOW x NON_POSITIVE) as
SIGNAL_CANDIDATE via RECOGNIZED_CANDIDATES -- this only widens which
regime_state strings this engine reports as a signal; direction is still
decided nowhere in this file (that remains .23's separately-reviewed
VALIDATED_LONG_ENTRY_REGIME_LABELS / VALIDATED_SHORT_ENTRY_REGIME_LABELS).

Adds required-vs-optional symbol handling so any symbol .12 reports (not
just BTC/ETH) gets its own decision: BTC/USD and ETH/USD remain the only
symbols that can block the whole decision if missing/invalid
(REQUIRED_SYMBOLS); every other symbol validates or blocks independently
(optional_symbols_blocked), mirroring the pattern already shipped in .12.

print_report() now iterates the decisions actually produced instead of a
fixed BTC/ETH tuple, and labels each symbol REQUIRED/OPTIONAL in the report.

Downstream-critical reason strings (FROZEN_CANDIDATE_MATCH /
FROZEN_CANDIDATE_NOT_PRESENT) and the existing FROZEN_CANDIDATE-only
consistency check against .12's frozen_candidate_match flag are preserved
unchanged, since .14's verify_candidate_consistency() checks them literally.

Adds 10 contract tests covering both-candidate recognition, the
CANDIDATE_MATCH_INCONSISTENT guard for each candidate, required-symbol
fail-closed behavior, optional-symbol non-cascading blocking, and the
updated print_report() output. Full existing suite (21 tests) still green.

